# Mapgen · osu!mania ranking criteria

When changing chart generation, enforce playability from
https://osu.ppy.sh/wiki/en/Ranking_criteria/osu!mania

## Hard rules (must never violate)

- **Auto must FC** — no object placement that makes Auto fail.
- **One object per column per timestamp**
- **No body overlap** — no rice/LN head inside an active hold; head may start on release
- **No empty columns** — every key in the keymode must be used (`ensureColumnCoverage`)
- **Chord cap** — respect tier `maxChordSize` (≤6 for Insane-or-lower)
- Always run `sanitizeManiaNotes` before write/export

## Music correlation (Overall guideline)

- Prefer **onset/beat-driven hit times** (`buildMusicalHitTimes`) over filling every snap
- Quiet sections should keep fewer / stronger onsets
- Do not invent timestamps with no audio support when onsets exist

## Diff-tier patterning (by dan strength, not difficulty names)

Use `resolveTierConstraints` / `filterTargetsForTier`:

| Tier | Approx dans | Caps |
|------|-------------|------|
| low | Regular 0–2, LN 3–4 | chord≤3, no bracket, weak/no jack, LN≥1/2 beat, release gap |
| mid | Regular 3–6, LN 5–7 | chord≤4, limited jacks, LN≥1/4 beat, chord gaps |
| high | Regular 7+, LN 8+ | chord≤6, freer patterns, LN≥1/12 beat |

- Cap jack runs with `maxJackRun`
- Space chords in streams with `chordMinGapBeats`
- Clamp `snapDivisor` to `maxSnapDivisor`

## LN

- Min length from tier (`minLnBeats`)
- Absorb same-column notes into LN bodies; never stack illegal rice

## Tempo

- Do not invent noisy multi-BPM maps when confidence is low
- SV scroll normalisation is still TODO
